{"path":"numeric/complex/tanh","title":"std::tanh(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>tanh<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::complex)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/tanh","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex hyperbolic tangent of a complex value z.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> tanh<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex hyperbolic tangent of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, complex hyperbolic tangent of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling_and_special_values\">Error handling and special values</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported consistent with <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/math_errhandling\">math_errhandling</a></span>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic,\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+0,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(+0,+0)</code>.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,+∞)</code> (for any<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\">[1]</a></sup> finite x), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> is raised.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,NaN)</code> (for any<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\">[2]</a></sup> finite x), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,y)</code> (for any finite positive y), the result is <code>(1,+0)</code>.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(1,±0)</code> (the sign of the imaginary part is unspecified).\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(1,±0)</code> (the sign of the imaginary part is unspecified).\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,+0)</code>.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,y)</code> (for any non-zero y), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>.\n</li></ul>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">per <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG14/www/docs/n1892.htm#dr_471\" data-external=\"1\">C11 DR471</a>, this only holds for non-zero x. If <code>z</code> is <code>(0,∞)</code>, the result should be <code>(0,NaN)</code>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">per <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG14/www/docs/n1892.htm#dr_471\" data-external=\"1\">C11 DR471</a>, this only holds for non-zero x. If <code>z</code> is <code>(0,NaN)</code>, the result should be <code>(0,NaN)</code>.</span>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\nMathematical definition of hyperbolic tangent is <span class=\"texhtml\">tanh z = <span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>e<span class=\"t-su\">z<br></span>-e<span class=\"t-su\">-z<br></span></td></tr><tr><td>e<span class=\"t-su\">z<br></span>+e<span class=\"t-su\">-z<br></span></td></tr></table></span></span>.\n<p>Hyperbolic tangent is an analytical function on the complex plane and has no branch cuts. It is periodic with respect to the imaginary component, with period πi, and has poles of the first order along the imaginary line, at coordinates <span class=\"texhtml\">(0, π(1/2 + n))</span>. However no common floating-point representation is able to represent <span class=\"texhtml\">π/2</span> exactly, thus there is no value of the argument for which a pole error occurs.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// behaves like real tanh along the real line</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"tanh\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (tanh(1) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// behaves like tangent along the imaginary line</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"tanh\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"><span class=\"kw1350\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tanh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" ( tan(1) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tan\"><span class=\"kw1343\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>tanh(1.000000,0.000000) = (0.761594,0.000000) (tanh(1) = 0.761594)\ntanh(0.000000,1.000000) = (0.000000,1.557408) ( tan(1) = 1.557408)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/sinh\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sinh<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes hyperbolic sine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\sinh{z}}\">sinh(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/cosh\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>cosh<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes hyperbolic cosine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\cosh{z}}\">cosh(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/atanh\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atanh<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes area hyperbolic tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\operatorname{artanh}{z}}\">artanh(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tanh</span><span>tanhf</span><span>tanhl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes hyperbolic tangent (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\tanh{x}}\">tanh(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/tanh\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tanh<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tanh\">std::tanh</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/ctanh\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>ctanh</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling and special values","id":"Error_handling_and_special_values"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::tanh(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Computes complex hyperbolic tangent of a complex value z."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, complex hyperbolic tangent of z is returned."},{"label":"Error handling and special values","note":"Errors are reported consistent with math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Mathematical definition of hyperbolic tangent is"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"sinh(std::complex)","note":"computes hyperbolic sine of a complex number (sinh(z))"},{"label":"cosh(std::complex)","note":"computes hyperbolic cosine of a complex number (cosh(z))"},{"label":"atanh(std::complex)","note":"computes area hyperbolic tangent of a complex number (artanh(z))"},{"label":"tanh, tanhf, tanhl","note":"computes hyperbolic tangent (tanh(x))"},{"label":"tanh(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::tanh to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":454,"codeBlockCount":2}
